---
// Static figure: how the bore of a cong was made, as a vertical section through the jade. A tubular drill, turned with
// wet sand as the abrasive, cuts a ring from one end to about halfway; the piece is turned over and drilled from the
// other end; the two rings meet, the core is broken out, and where they did not line up exactly a small step is left
// near the middle. After the Freer's account of Liangzhu perforations drilled from two sides; the AIC suggests a bamboo
// tube as the drill. Simple drawings, not a reconstruction of any one workshop. Step layout, three columns.
---
<figure class="glass-steps three">
  <ol>
    <li>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 160 120" aria-hidden="true">
        <rect class="db-jade" x="44" y="22" width="72" height="88" />
        <rect class="db-tube" x="64" y="4" width="4" height="58" />
        <rect class="db-tube" x="92" y="4" width="4" height="58" />
        <path class="db-cut" d="M64 22 V62 M68 22 V62 M92 22 V62 M96 22 V62" />
        <path class="db-sand" d="M60 18 h2 M100 17 h2 M58 21 h1.5 M103 20 h1.5 M62 15 h1.5" />
        <path class="db-turn" d="M70 10 A10 4 0 1 0 90 10" />
      </svg>
      <p><strong>从一端磨下去</strong>一根空心的管子压在玉上转动，管口和玉之间加湿砂。真正在磨玉的是比玉更硬的砂，管子只是带着砂转。磨出一道环形的槽，大约到一半深。</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 160 120" aria-hidden="true">
        <rect class="db-jade" x="44" y="10" width="72" height="88" />
        <path class="db-cut db-done" d="M64 10 V50 M68 10 V50 M92 10 V50 M96 10 V50" />
        <rect class="db-tube" x="70" y="58" width="4" height="58" />
        <rect class="db-tube" x="98" y="58" width="4" height="58" />
        <path class="db-cut" d="M70 98 V58 M74 98 V58 M98 98 V58 M102 98 V58" />
        <path class="db-turn" d="M76 112 A10 4 0 1 1 96 112" />
      </svg>
      <p><strong>翻过来，从另一端磨</strong>再从另一端对准着磨。两次很难对得分毫不差，两道槽在中间相遇时，常常错开一点。</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 160 120" aria-hidden="true">
        <path class="db-jade" d="M44 16 H64 V56 H70 V104 H44 Z" />
        <path class="db-jade" d="M96 16 H116 V104 H102 V56 H96 Z" />
        <circle class="db-mark" cx="67" cy="56" r="8" />
        <circle class="db-mark" cx="99" cy="56" r="8" />
      </svg>
      <p><strong>取出芯子，留下台阶</strong>两道槽打通后，中间的圆柱形芯子就能取出来。孔壁在中间留下一道小小的台阶（圆圈处）。良渚玉器上这样两面对钻留下的痕迹，是研究者辨认其制作方法的线索之一。</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <figcaption>示意图：管钻两面对钻的过程，比例和错位都有夸大；不代表某一件玉器或某一个作坊的具体做法。良渚人用的钻管是什么材料，研究者有不同的推测（如竹管）。</figcaption>
</figure>
